WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:06.660
Multi-tenant and multi-project RAG systems need strict separation across the full operating environment.

2
00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:12.680
Tenant context should be enforced by trusted server-side code, not chosen by the client.

3
00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:21.260
A user interface may display a selected tenant or project, but the authorization decision should come from verified identity, membership, and policy state.

4
00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:24.420
Isolation choices appear throughout the pipeline.

5
00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:30.200
Some organizations use per-tenant document stores, indexes, and caches.

6
00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:36.940
Others use shared infrastructure with strict tenant filters and careful operational controls.

7
00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:47.680
Either pattern requires explicit rules for storage, retrieval, prompt assembly, logs, traces, exports, analytics, backups, and administrative tooling.

8
00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:52.340
A boundary that exists in the index but not in logs or exports is not complete.

9
00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:55.500
Debugging convenience can become a leakage path.

10
00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:58.560
Support dashboards may show retrieved chunks.

11
00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:00.740
Trace views may capture prompts.

12
00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:04.120
Admin tools may let operators browse indexes.

13
00:01:04.220 --> 00:01:08.140
Export features may include citations or transcripts.

14
00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:13.040
Cached prompts and responses may retain sensitive material after the source access changed.

15
00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:17.780
These surfaces deserve the same permission thinking as the user-facing answer.

16
00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:22.940
Tenant isolation should be verified before onboarding sensitive users or datasets.

17
00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:33.280
Tests should prove that one tenant cannot retrieve, cite, log, export, or view another tenant's material through normal features or operational tooling.

18
00:01:33.380 --> 00:01:36.340
Isolation is not only a storage design.

19
00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:41.400
It is a full-system property that includes how people operate and troubleshoot the platform.
